<http://example.org/whu#BioChemicalExperiment> <http://example.org/whu#prompt> "### Define\nBiochemical/chemical experimental plan: treated specimens → measurement DataSet.\n### Context\nAssays, digestion–instrument runs, wet-lab analyses. Has Goal targeting TargetAnalyte.\n### Links\nisPrecededBy SpecimenPreprocessing (typical);\nResearchStep -isStepOfPlan→ BioChemicalExperiment;\nhasInputVar ProcessedSpecimen; hasOutputVar DataSet;\nhasGoal → Goal.\n### Examples\n\"Hg determination by ICP-MS\"; \"MeHg extraction and analysis\"."@en .
<http://example.org/whu#TargetVariable> <http://example.org/whu#prompt> "### Define\nStatistical or modeled variable estimated in ComputationalExperiment.\n### Examples\n\"Hg content\"; \"hazard quotient\"; \"bioaccumulation factor\".\n### Links\nGoal -hasTarget→ TargetVariable; DataSet/ScalarMeasurementDatum -iao:is_about→ TargetVariable."@en .
<http://example.org/whu#Specimen> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Specimen"@en .
<http://example.org/whu#hasDuration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/whu#ExecutionEnvironment> .
<http://purl.org/net/p-plan#isStepOfPlan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/whu#ResearchStep> .
<http://example.org/whu#Specimen> <http://example.org/whu#prompt> "### Define\nPhysical sample collected from an environment before or without full preprocessing.\n### Context\nMust be traceable to EnvironmentFeature; typically output of SpecimenCollection ResearchStep.\n### Examples\n\"rice grains\"; \"fish tissue\"; \"soil cores\"; \"river water samples\".\n### Links\nResearchStep(Collection) -hasOutputVar→ Specimen;\nResearchStep(Preprocessing) -hasInputVar→ Specimen;\nSpecimen -wasDerivedFrom→ EnvironmentFeature."@en .
