<http://example.org/whu#hasExecutionEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Plan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Plan"@en .
<http://example.org/whu#hasTarget> <http://example.org/whu#prompt> "Define: A Goal targets a TargetObject (analyte or variable).\nExamples: \"quantify Hg in rice\" → hasTarget(goal, TargetAnalyte:Hg)."@en .
<http://purl.org/net/p-plan#correspondsToStep> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> .
_:n73f149ee62ab420da56059eeebd4be50b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasPart> <http://example.org/whu#prompt> "Define: DataSet contains DataItem / ScalarMeasurementDatum.\nExamples: \"Dataset S1 includes Cd concentration measurements\" → hasPart(DataSet, ScalarMeasurementDatum)."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://example.org/whu#EnvironmentFeature> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <http://example.org/whu#prompt> "Define: Specimen derived from EnvironmentFeature; ProcessedSpecimen derived from Specimen.\nExamples: \"Rice grains collected from paddy soil\" → wasDerivedFrom(Specimen, EnvironmentFeature)."@en .
<http://purl.org/mp#Claim> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Claim"@en .
<http://example.org/whu#Specimen> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Collected biological or environmental specimen (physical carrier)."@en .
<http://purl.org/mp#Statement> <http://example.org/whu#prompt> "### Define\nA scientific proposition or factual assertion (not necessarily the terminal Claim).\n### Context\nExtract complete propositions in Results/Discussion that mediate between evidence and Claim.\n### Examples\n\"MeHg in grains decreased under biochar treatment\".\n### Links\nStatement ∈ SupportGraph; Statement ← supports — ScienceEvidence."@en .
<http://example.org/whu#Software> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_InformationContentEntity> .
<http://purl.org/net/p-plan#hasInputVar> <http://example.org/whu#prompt> "Define: ResearchStep consumes Specimen, ProcessedSpecimen or DataSet as typed input.\nExamples: \"ICP-MS used digested solutions\" → hasInputVar(step, ProcessedSpecimen)."@en .
<http://purl.org/mp#Data> <http://example.org/whu#prompt> "### Define\nArgumentative data element that can support or challenge Statement/Claim.\nPrefer creating whu:DataSet for structured scientific datasets; use mp:Data only when a more specific subclass does not apply."@en .
<http://purl.org/mp#statement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<http://example.org/whu#hasHumidity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://example.org/whu#ExecutionEnvironment> .
<http://purl.org/mp#Method> <http://example.org/whu#prompt> "### Define\nA named method, protocol or standard referenced in experiments.\n### Context\nExtract explicit method names/standards (EPA 3052, ICP-MS protocol, statistical test names).\n### Examples\n\"following EPA Method 3052\"; \"analyzed by ICP-MS\".\n### Links\nResearchStep -declaredUsed→ Method; Method ∈ ScienceEvidence via prov:hadMember."@en .
<http://purl.org/net/p-plan#hasInputVar> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/whu#BioChemicalExperiment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Plan> .
_:n73f149ee62ab420da56059eeebd4be50b7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<http://example.org/whu#EnvironmentFeature> <http://example.org/whu#prompt> "### Define\nPhysical, ecological or geographic context: soil, water, site, region, climate condition.\n### Context\nExtract named locations, environmental media, site types. Align to ENVO/GeoNames when possible (skos:closeMatch).\nOptional: geo:lat, geo:long, geo:alt, gn:parentFeature.\n### Examples\n\"paddy soil in Nanjing\"; \"river delta\"; \"urban air\".\n### Links\nSpecimenCollection -hasContext→ EnvironmentFeature; Specimen -wasDerivedFrom→ EnvironmentFeature."@en .
